## Configuration

```toml
# config.toml
[user]
timezone = "Asia/Shanghai"
display_name = "qearl"

[llm]
provider = "anthropic"
model    = "claude-opus-4-7"
base_url = "${ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL:-}"
api_key  = "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}"
thinking_level = "medium"

[embedding]
provider = "gemini"
model    = "gemini-embedding-002"          # multimodal
base_url = "${GEMINI_BASE_URL:-}"
api_key  = "${GEMINI_API_KEY}"
fallback = "fts5"

[stt]
provider = "gemini"
model    = "gemini-2.5-flash"
base_url = "${GEMINI_BASE_URL:-}"
api_key  = "${GEMINI_API_KEY}"

[video_understanding]
provider = "gemini"
model    = "gemini-2.5-flash"
base_url = "${GEMINI_BASE_URL:-}"
api_key  = "${GEMINI_API_KEY}"
max_duration_seconds = 600

[tts]
provider = "openai"
model    = "tts-1-hd"
voice    = "shimmer"
base_url = "${OPENAI_BASE_URL:-}"
api_key  = "${OPENAI_API_KEY}"

[image_gen]
provider = "openai"
model    = "gpt-image-1"
base_url = "${OPENAI_BASE_URL:-}"
api_key  = "${OPENAI_API_KEY}"

[discord]
token = "${DISCORD_TOKEN}"

[side_door]
mode        = "tailscale-only"             # tailscale-only | bearer | public-2fa
bind        = "100.x.x.x"                  # Tailscale IP (or 127.0.0.1 behind nginx)
port        = 7878
bearer      = "${FAMILIAR_BEARER:-}"
totp_secret = "${FAMILIAR_TOTP_SECRET:-}"

[mac_sidecar]
url    = "http://100.x.x.x:7879"
bearer = "${MAC_SIDECAR_BEARER}"
```

---

## System prompt slot order (cache-stable)

```
[hardcoded base instructions]                    stable
[SOUL.md]                                        stable (you edit)
[USER.md]                                        stable (you edit)
[tools index]                                    stable per session
[MEMORY.md]                                      semi-stable (agent edits)
─── cache breakpoint ───
[recent context, author-tagged + ISO timestamps] volatile
[<recall>top-K from RAG</recall>]                volatile, injected via transformContext
[new user message]                               volatile
```

---

## Stages — build order

Each stage produces a runnable bot. Don't move on until the prior stage works end-to-end.

### Stage 1 — Skeleton (~1 evening)
- `package.json`, `tsconfig`, `biome`, `.env.example`, `config.example.toml`
- `src/config.ts` — load + env interpolation
- `src/persona.ts` — load SOUL.md + USER.md
- `src/agent.ts` — construct Agent with system prompt assembled from base + SOUL + USER
- `src/discord.ts` — gateway connection, message → AgentMessage, basic reply
- **Done when:** you can DM the bot and it replies, with your custom persona.

### Stage 2 — Logging + short-term context (~1 evening)
- SQLite schema: `messages`, `attachments`
- Append every inbound and outbound message to `data/memory.db`
- Author-tagged ISO timestamps wrapping each message in context
- pi-agent-core's compaction handles in-context window
- **Done when:** all conversations persist; context survives restarts.

### Stage 3 — Long-term RAG (~2 evenings)
- `src/memory/embed.ts` — Gemini multimodal adapter (text only first)
- Async embedding worker writes vectors to `embeddings` table
- `src/memory/recall.ts` — hybrid search (vec + FTS5), recency decay, top-K
- Wire into `Agent.transformContext` with hard 150ms timeout
- **Done when:** agent recalls older conversations relevant to your current message.

### Stage 4 — Lossless-claw summaries (~2 evenings)
- `src/memory/compact.ts` — periodic summary roll-up worker
- `summaries` + `summary_links` tables
- `recall_detail(summary_id)` tool returns linked raw messages
- Summaries also embedded and recall-eligible
- **Done when:** old conversations compact gracefully; agent can drill from summary → raw on demand.

### Stage 5 — Bash + side-door HTTP (~1 evening)
- `src/tools/bash.ts` — YOLO shell, no sandbox
- `src/tools/memory.ts` — remember/forget/memory_search/recall_detail
- `src/side-door/server.ts` — HTTP + WebSocket, auth.ts pluggable
- Routes: `/msg` `/event` `/channels/:id/log` `/status` `/thinking/:id` `/stream`
- **Done when:** agent can run bash; you can `curl POST /msg` to talk to it without Discord.

### Stage 6 — WebUI front-end (~1 evening)
- `web/index.html` `web/app.js` `web/style.css`
- WebSocket subscription to `/stream`
- Channel picker, message input, attachment upload
- "Web" appears as its own channel in agent's context
- **Done when:** you can talk to the agent from your phone browser via Tailscale.

### Stage 7 — TTS + image-gen tools (~1 evening)
- `src/tools/tts.ts` — text → mp3, attached to next reply
- `src/tools/image_gen.ts` — prompt → png, attached to next reply
- **Done when:** "say hi out loud" produces a voice message; "draw me a sunset" produces an image.

### Stage 8 — STT + video understanding intake (~1 evening)
- `src/intake/stt.ts` — Gemini transcribes voice attachments
- `src/intake/video.ts` — Gemini describes video attachments
- Transcripts/descriptions injected into the message text before agent sees it
- **Done when:** sending a voice memo or short video gets a sensible reply.

### Stage 9 — Mac sidecar (~2 evenings, separate repo)
- New repo `familiar-mac`
- HTTP server, Tailscale-bound, bearer auth
- Endpoints: `/cdp/navigate` `/cdp/eval` `/cdp/read_visible` `/cdp/screenshot` `/screen` `/exec`
- launchd plist for start-at-login
- Chrome wrapper script that always launches with `--remote-debugging-port=9222`
- **Done when:** Mac sidecar is reachable from VPS over Tailscale; CDP attaches to your real Chrome.

### Stage 10 — `mac.*` tool client (~½ evening)
- `src/tools/mac.ts` — thin HTTP wrappers for each sidecar endpoint
- Surfaced as agent tools
- **Done when:** "go to twitter and tell me what's on the timeline" works.

### Stage 11 — Install + service + docs (~1 evening)
- `familiar init <workspace>` — scaffold config, stub files, generate bearer + TOTP secrets
- `familiar run <workspace>` — foreground for testing
- `familiar install-service <workspace>` — write systemd unit, enable
- `scripts/nginx-public-2fa.conf.example` — reference for public-mode users
- README with deploy walkthrough
- **Done when:** a fresh Debian VPS goes from `apt install` to running daemon in <10 min.

**Total:** ~14 evenings (~2–3 weeks part-time).

---

## Key decisions (locked)

- **No fork.** pi-agent-core + pi-ai as npm deps. Track upstream effortlessly.
- **Two processes**, not one: `familiar` (VPS) + `familiar-mac` (Mac).
- **Single global `MEMORY.md`** — no per-channel split.
- **RAG and lossless-claw summaries from v0** — long-term memory is load-bearing.
- **One Gemini key** for embeddings, STT, video understanding — multimodal, consistent.
- **WebUI in v0** as Discord-down fallback, not Phase 3.
- **Side-door auth modes** config-switchable: tailscale-only | bearer | public-2fa.
- **YOLO bash** on VPS. No sandbox. User's machine, user's call.
- **COT reactive**, not always-shown. 🧠 reaction or `why?` reply reveals as spoiler-tagged thread.
- **Reactive only in v0.** Proactive triggers (cron, presence) deferred — but `/event` endpoint shaped to accept them additively.
- **Web is its own channel** in the agent's context, parallel to Discord channels. MEMORY/RAG global, conversation thread per channel.
- **Author-tagged ISO timestamps** on all messages, on the volatile side of the cache breakpoint.

---

## Deferred to post-v0

- Group-chat collect/debounce mode (DM-first works without it)
- Bot-to-bot anti-loop (only relevant in shared bot channels)
- Proactive triggers: cron-based greetings, decay-based outreach, Mac signals, Discord presence
- iOS Shortcuts presence webhook (architecture-ready via `/event`, just no consumer yet)
- Polished webUI built on `pi-web-ui` components (v0 ships vanilla HTML)
- Skill auto-discovery (pi-chat-style)
- Voice channel TTS playback (audio attachment pattern covers it)
- Cost cap / token budget controls
- Subagent tool

